{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00763",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.98,
      "end_seconds": 9.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "G'day. Um, I'm bloated. Like permanently. And windy. It's been weeks. I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.91,
      "end_seconds": 15.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "How many weeks, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.79,
      "end_seconds": 31.15,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "Oh, I don't know. Maybe, hang on, I wrote it down. Anyway, a few weeks. Or longer. I can't pin the start."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.11,
      "end_seconds": 38.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "That's fine. Is it there all day, or after certain foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.56,
      "end_seconds": 49.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "By the afternoon, it's like I've swallowed a football. Better in the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.52,
      "end_seconds": 56.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Any weight loss, or change in your appetite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.23,
      "end_seconds": 64.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "No. Weight's the same. Appetite's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.13,
      "end_seconds": 71.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Any blood in your stools, or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.9,
      "end_seconds": 76.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No. No blood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.4,
      "end_seconds": 83.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Any change in your bowels, constipation, looseness? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.23,
      "end_seconds": 95.71,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Bit of both, depending on the day. Nothing out of the ordinary for me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.52,
      "end_seconds": 101.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Any pain, or vomiting? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.61,
      "end_seconds": 109.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Some mild cramps now and then. No vomiting. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.46,
      "end_seconds": 122.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "And any trouble with your waterworks, or anything gynaecological, pelvic pain or a change in your periods? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.95,
      "end_seconds": 128.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "No. All normal. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.12,
      "end_seconds": 138.14,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "Let me press your tummy. Lie back on the couch for me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.03,
      "end_seconds": 144.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Sure. Is this going to hurt? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.59,
      "end_seconds": 168.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Not if I can help it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.99,
      "end_seconds": 182.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.78,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, and I can feel it's bloated and a little tight, but it's not tender, and I can't feel any lumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.63,
      "end_seconds": 188.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Is that good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.91,
      "end_seconds": 197.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "It's what I'd hoped. Any breathlessness, chest pain, or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.16,
      "end_seconds": 203.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.62,
      "end_seconds": 224.64,
      "duration_seconds": 18.02,
      "text": "Right. Bloating that comes on through the day, with a bit of both loose and hard stools, fits with irritable bowel, but I can't rule out something like coeliac disease or lactose intolerance."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.36,
      "end_seconds": 231.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "How do you find out? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.99,
      "end_seconds": 241.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "Often by keeping a food diary, and trying changes one by one. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.35,
      "end_seconds": 246.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "A food diary, I could try. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.84,
      "end_seconds": 257.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Write down what you eat, when the bloating comes, and your bowel habits, for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.55,
      "end_seconds": 265.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Right. And what should I eat? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.83,
      "end_seconds": 278.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "Regular meals, eat slowly, avoid fizzy drinks and chewing gum, and cut down on beans, onions, and sweeteners."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.7,
      "end_seconds": 285.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Ah, I do love my sugar-free gum. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.41,
      "end_seconds": 291.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "That could be a culprit, actually. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.72,
      "end_seconds": 299.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Well, I'll stop that and see. Thanks, doc. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.39,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Hope it settles. ~"
    }
  ]
}
